{
  "kanda": "bala",
  "sarga": 38,
  "title": "The legend of emperor Sagara",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga38/balasans38.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga38/balaitrans38.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Sage Vishvamitra narrates the legend of Sagara, the earliest King of Ayodhya and Rama's forefather, who is childless, but who begets sixty thousand sons of merit and one son of demerit. Emperor Sagara is the one who brought celestial Ganga onto the surface of earth.."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकिरामायणे आदिकाव्ये बालकाण्डे अष्टात्रिंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 38th chapter in Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1.38.1",
      "label": "1.38.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "तां कथां कौशिको रामे निवेद्य मधुराक्षरम् |\nपुन रेवापरं वाक्यं काकुत्स्थमिदमब्रवीत्",
      "iast": "tām kathām kauśiko rāme nivedya madhura akṣaram |\npunaḥ eva aparam vākyam kākutstham idam abravīt",
      "translation": "Describing that legend of Kaartikeya to Rama, the descendent of Kaushi, namely sage Vishvamitra has further spoken this best sentence worded melodiously to Rama, the descendent of Kakutstha.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "kaushikaH",
          "iast": "kauśikaḥ",
          "devanagari": "कौशिकः",
          "meaning": "descendent of Kaushika, Vishvamitra",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "taam kathaam",
          "iast": "tām kathām",
          "devanagari": "तां कथां",
          "meaning": "that, legend of Kaarthikeya",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raame nivedya",
          "iast": "rāme nivedya",
          "devanagari": "रामे निवेद्य",
          "meaning": "in Rama, to Rama, on submitting - describing",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "punaH eva",
          "iast": "punaḥ eva",
          "devanagari": "पुनः एव",
          "meaning": "again, thus - further",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "idam aparam vaakyam",
          "iast": "idam aparam vākyam",
          "devanagari": "इदं अपरं वाक्यं",
          "meaning": ", this, best, sentence",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "madhura akSaram",
          "iast": "madhura akṣaram",
          "devanagari": "मधुर अक्षरं",
          "meaning": "in melodious, words",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kaakutstham abraviit",
          "iast": "kākutstham abravīt",
          "devanagari": "काकुत्स्थं अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "to Rama of Kakutstha, spoke.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.2",
      "label": "1.38.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "अयोध्याधिपतिर्वीरः पूर्वमासीन्नराधिपः |\nसगरो नाम धर्मात्मा प्रजाकामः स चाप्रजः",
      "iast": "ayodhyā adhipatiḥ vīraḥ pūrvam āsīt narādhipaḥ |\nsagaro nāma dharmātmā prajākāmaḥ sa ca aprajaḥ",
      "translation": "\"Once there was a valiant an virtue-souled king of Ayodhya named Sagara, who is without offspring, as such he was longing for offspring.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "puurvam",
          "iast": "pūrvam",
          "devanagari": "पूर्वं",
          "meaning": "once upon a time",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ayodhyaa adhipatiH",
          "iast": "ayodhyā adhipatiḥ",
          "devanagari": "अयोध्या अधिपतिः",
          "meaning": "Ayodhya's, king",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "viiraH dharmaatmaa",
          "iast": "vīraḥ dharmātmā",
          "devanagari": "वीरः धर्मात्मा",
          "meaning": "valiant one, virtue-souled one",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sagaraH naama",
          "iast": "sagaraḥ nāma",
          "devanagari": "सगरः नाम",
          "meaning": "Sagara, renowned as",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saH",
          "iast": "saḥ",
          "devanagari": "सः",
          "meaning": "he was",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "a prajaH",
          "iast": "a prajaḥ",
          "devanagari": "अ प्रजः",
          "meaning": "without, offspring",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 12
        },
        {
          "itrans": "prajaa kaamaH ca",
          "iast": "prajā kāmaḥ ca",
          "devanagari": "प्रजा कामः च",
          "meaning": "offspring, longing for, also.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.3",
      "label": "1.38.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "वैदर्भदुहिता राम केशिनी नाम नामतः |\nज्येष्ठा सगरपत्नी सा धर्मिष्ठा सत्यवादिनी",
      "iast": "vaidarbha duhitā rāma keśinī nāma nāmataḥ |\njyeṣṭhā sagara patnī sā dharmiṣṭhā satya vādinī",
      "translation": "\"The daughter of King of Vidarbha, renowned by name Keshini, is the eldest wife of Sagara, and she was virtue-minded, and an advocate of truth.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raamaH",
          "iast": "rāmaḥ",
          "devanagari": "रामः",
          "meaning": "oh, Rama",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaidarbha duhitaa",
          "iast": "vaidarbha duhitā",
          "devanagari": "वैदर्भ दुहिता",
          "meaning": "Vidarbha [king of], daughter",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "naamataH keshinii naama",
          "iast": "nāmataḥ keśinī nāma",
          "devanagari": "नामतः केशिनी नाम",
          "meaning": "by name, Keshini, renowned as",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "jyeSThaa sagara patnii",
          "iast": "jyeṣṭhā sagara patnī",
          "devanagari": "ज्येष्ठा सगर पत्नी",
          "meaning": "elder, Sagara's, wife",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saa dharma iSThaa satya vaadinii",
          "iast": "sā dharma iṣṭhā satya vādinī",
          "devanagari": "सा धर्म इष्ठा सत्य वादिनी",
          "meaning": "she is, virtue, minded, truth, advocate of.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.4",
      "label": "1.38.4",
      "numbers": [
        4
      ],
      "devanagari": "अरिष्ठनेमिदुहिता सुपर्णभगिनी तु सा |\nद्वितीया सगरस्यासीत् पत्नी सुमतिसंज्ञिता",
      "iast": "ariṣṭhanemi duhitā suparṇa bhaginī tu sā |\ndvitīyā sagarasya āsīt patnī sumati saṃGYitā",
      "translation": "\"The daughter of Arishtanemi, namely sage Kashyapa, and who is also the sister of Garuda, the Divine-Eagle-vehicle of Vishnu, is the second wife of Sagara, who is known by the name Sumati.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "ariSThanemeH duhitaa",
          "iast": "ariṣṭhanemeḥ duhitā",
          "devanagari": "अरिष्ठनेमेः दुहिता",
          "meaning": "Arishtanemi's, daughter",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "suparNa bhaginii tu",
          "iast": "suparṇa bhaginī tu",
          "devanagari": "सुपर्ण भगिनी तु",
          "meaning": "Garuda's, sister, on her part",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sumati samGYitaa",
          "iast": "sumati samGYitā",
          "devanagari": "सुमति सम्GYइता",
          "meaning": "Sumati, indicated by - designated by that name",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saa sagarasya",
          "iast": "sā sagarasya",
          "devanagari": "सा सगरस्य",
          "meaning": "she is of Sagara",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dvitiiyaa patnii aasiit",
          "iast": "dvitīyā patnī āsīt",
          "devanagari": "द्वितीया पत्नी आसीत्",
          "meaning": "second, wife, was there.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.5",
      "label": "1.38.5",
      "numbers": [
        5
      ],
      "devanagari": "ताभ्यां सह महाराजा पत्नीभ्याम् तप्तवांस्तपः |\nहिमवंतं समासाद्य भृगुप्रस्रवणे गिरौ",
      "iast": "tābhyām saha mahārājā patnībhyām taptavān tapaḥ |\nhimavantam samāsādya bhṛgu prasravaṇe girau",
      "translation": "\"Reaching the Himalayan Mountains along with his two wives that great King Sagara practised asceticism on a mountain called Brugu-prsravana for progeny.",
      "notes": [
        "<em>The Mt. Brugu-prsravana is said to be among Himalayan range on which the kindness of Sage Bhrigu is ever- flowing.</em>"
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "taabhyaam patniibhyaam saha",
          "iast": "tābhyām patnībhyām saha",
          "devanagari": "ताभ्यां पत्नीभ्यां सह",
          "meaning": "with them two, with two wives, along with",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "[saH",
          "iast": "[saḥ",
          "devanagari": "[सः",
          "meaning": "he that]",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahaaraajaa",
          "iast": "mahārājā",
          "devanagari": "महाराजा",
          "meaning": "great-king",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "himavantam sam aasaadya",
          "iast": "himavantam sam āsādya",
          "devanagari": "हिमवन्तं सं आसाद्य",
          "meaning": "Himalayas, on well-reaching",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhR^igu pra sravaNe girau",
          "iast": "bhṛgu pra sravaṇe girau",
          "devanagari": "भृगु प्र स्रवणे गिरौ",
          "meaning": "on Brhugu-prasavana, mountain",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tapaH taptavaan",
          "iast": "tapaḥ taptavān",
          "devanagari": "तपः तप्तवान्",
          "meaning": "ascesis, he undertook",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.6",
      "label": "1.38.6",
      "numbers": [
        6
      ],
      "devanagari": "अथ वर्षशते पूर्णे तपसाराधितो मुनिः |\nसगराय वरं प्रादाद् भृगुः सत्यवतां वरः",
      "iast": "atha varṣa śate pūrṇe tapasā ārādhito muniḥ |\nsagarāya varam prādād bhṛguḥ satyavatām varaḥ",
      "translation": "\"On completion of a hundred years of ascesis, and when the Sage Bhrugu is worshipped with asceticism, that sage who is a prominent one among the patrons of truth bestowed a boon to Sagara.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "atha varSa shate puurNe",
          "iast": "atha varṣa śate pūrṇe",
          "devanagari": "अथ वर्ष शते पूर्णे",
          "meaning": "then, years, hundred, on completion of",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tapasaa aaraadhitaH",
          "iast": "tapasā ārādhitaḥ",
          "devanagari": "तपसा आराधितः",
          "meaning": "with asceticism, one who is worshipped",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "satyavataam varaH",
          "iast": "satyavatām varaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सत्यवतां वरः",
          "meaning": "among patrons of truth, prominent one",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhR^iguH muniH",
          "iast": "bhṛguḥ muniḥ",
          "devanagari": "भृगुः मुनिः",
          "meaning": "Bhrugu, the sage",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sagaraaya varam praadaad",
          "iast": "sagarāya varam prādād",
          "devanagari": "सगराय वरं प्रादाद्",
          "meaning": "to Sagara, boon, bestowed.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.7",
      "label": "1.38.7",
      "numbers": [
        7
      ],
      "devanagari": "अपत्यलाभः सुमहान् भविष्यति तवानघ |\nकीर्तिं चाप्रतिमां लोके प्राप्स्यसे पुरुषर्षभ",
      "iast": "apatya lābhaḥ sumahān bhaviṣyati tava anagha |\nkīrtim ca apratimām loke prāpsyase puruṣarṣabha",
      "translation": "\" 'Oh, merited one, you will achieve very admirable progeny, and oh, best one among men, you will also acquire an unparalleled renown in the world.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "anagha",
          "iast": "anagha",
          "devanagari": "अनघ",
          "meaning": "oh, merited one",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
