    {
      "id": "1.38.10",
      "label": "1.38.10",
      "numbers": [
        10
      ],
      "devanagari": "एकः कस्याः सुतो ब्रह्मन् का बहून् जनयिष्यति |\nश्रोतुमिच्छावहे ब्रह्मन् सत्यमस्तु वचस्तव",
      "iast": "ekaḥ kasyāḥ suto brahman kā bahūn janayiṣyati |\nśrotum icchāvahe brahman satyam astu vacaḥ tava",
      "translation": "\" 'Which of us will carry one son, oh, Brahma-sage, and which of us begets numerous sons, we two wish to listen about that, oh, Brahman, let your word betide truth.' Thus, the queens of Sagara spoke to the sage.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "brahman",
          "iast": "brahman",
          "devanagari": "ब्रह्मन्",
          "meaning": "oh, Brahma-sage",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kasyaaH ekaH sutaH",
          "iast": "kasyāḥ ekaḥ sutaḥ",
          "devanagari": "कस्याः एकः सुतः",
          "meaning": "to whom, one, son - will be there",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "brahman",
          "iast": "brahman",
          "devanagari": "ब्रह्मन्",
          "meaning": "oh, Brahman",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shrotum icChaavahe",
          "iast": "śrotum icchāvahe",
          "devanagari": "श्रोतुं इच्छावहे",
          "meaning": "to listen, we two wish to",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tava vacaH satyam astu",
          "iast": "tava vacaḥ satyam astu",
          "devanagari": "तव वचः सत्यं अस्तु",
          "meaning": "your, word, let come, true.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.11",
      "label": "1.38.11",
      "numbers": [
        11
      ],
      "devanagari": "तयोस्तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा भृगुः परमधार्मिकः |\nउवाच परमां वाणीं स्वच्छन्दोऽत्र विधीयताम्",
      "iast": "tayoḥ tat vacanam śrutvā bhṛguḥ paramadhārmikaḥ |\nuvāca paramām vāṇīm svacchando atra vidhīyatām",
      "translation": "On listening their words the Sage Bhrigu spoke in a glorious tone, 'let your freewill be brought to bear this issue.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "parama dhaarmikaH bhR^iguH",
          "iast": "parama dhārmikaḥ bhṛguḥ",
          "devanagari": "परम धार्मिकः भृगुः",
          "meaning": "one with - sublime, sanctity, sage Bhrigu",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tayoH tat vacanam shrutvaa",
          "iast": "tayoḥ tat vacanam śrutvā",
          "devanagari": "तयोः तत् वचनं श्रुत्वा",
          "meaning": "of their, words, on listening",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "paramaam vaaNiim uvaaca",
          "iast": "paramām vāṇīm uvāca",
          "devanagari": "परमां वाणीं उवाच",
          "meaning": "with glorious, tone, spoke",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "atra",
          "iast": "atra",
          "devanagari": "अत्र",
          "meaning": "in this matter - this issue",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "svacChandaH vidhiiyataam",
          "iast": "svacchandaḥ vidhīyatām",
          "devanagari": "स्वच्छन्दः विधीयतां",
          "meaning": "[your] freewill, be brought to bear - you may exercise.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.12",
      "label": "1.38.12",
      "numbers": [
        12
      ],
      "devanagari": "एको वंशकरो वास्तु बहवो वा महाबलाः |\nकीर्तिमन्तो महोत्साहाः का वा कं वरमिच्छति",
      "iast": "eko vaṃśa karo vā astu bahavo vā mahābalāḥ |\nkīrtimanto mahotsāhāḥ kā vā kam varam icchati",
      "translation": "\" 'Whether one wants one son who enriches dynasty, or whether numerous sons who will be highly energetic, highly renowned, and highly enthusiastic. Who wants which boon from either of them?' Thus, the Sage gave them the option.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "vamsha karaH ekaH astu vaa",
          "iast": "vamśa karaḥ ekaḥ astu vā",
          "devanagari": "वम्श करः एकः अस्तु वा",
          "meaning": "dynasty, enriching, one son, there shall be, whether",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahaa balaaH",
          "iast": "mahā balāḥ",
          "devanagari": "महा बलाः",
          "meaning": "highly, energetic ones",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kiirtimantaH",
          "iast": "kīrtimantaḥ",
          "devanagari": "कीर्तिमन्तः",
          "meaning": "highly renowned ones",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahaa utsaahaaH",
          "iast": "mahā utsāhāḥ",
          "devanagari": "महा उत्साहाः",
          "meaning": "highly, enthusiastic ones",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bahavaH vaa",
          "iast": "bahavaḥ vā",
          "devanagari": "बहवः वा",
          "meaning": "numerous, whether",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kaa vaa",
          "iast": "kā vā",
          "devanagari": "का वा",
          "meaning": "who, either - among you two",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kam varam icChati",
          "iast": "kam varam icchati",
          "devanagari": "कं वरं इच्छति",
          "meaning": "what, boon, wanted.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.13",
      "label": "1.38.13",
      "numbers": [
        13
      ],
      "devanagari": "मुनेस्तु वचनं श्रुत्वा केशिनी रघुनंदन |\nपुत्रं वंशकरं राम जग्राह नृपसंनिधौ",
      "iast": "muneḥ tu vacanam śrutvā keśinī raghunandana |\nputram vaṃśa karam rāma jagrāha nṛpa saṃnidhau",
      "translation": "\"On listening the words of the sage, oh, Rama, oh, delighter of Raghu's dynasty, the first queen Keshini has chosen one son who enriches the dynasty in the presence of King Sagara. [1-38-13]]",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raghu nandana",
          "iast": "raghu nandana",
          "devanagari": "रघु नन्दन",
          "meaning": "oh, Raghu's, delight Rama",
