          "iast": "asamanja iti khyāta",
          "devanagari": "असमन्ज इति ख्यात",
          "meaning": "Asamanja, thus - known as",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "putram vyajaayata",
          "iast": "putram vyajāyata",
          "devanagari": "पुत्रं व्यजायत",
          "meaning": "to son, gave birth.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.38.17",
      "label": "1.38.17",
      "numbers": [
        17
      ],
      "devanagari": "सुमतिस्तु नरव्याघ्र गर्भतुंबं व्यजायत |\nषष्टिः पुत्रसहस्राणि तुंबभेदाद्विनिःसृताः",
      "iast": "sumatiḥ tu naravyāghra garbha tumbam vyajāyata |\nṣaṣṭiḥ putra sahasrāṇi tumba bhedāt viniḥsṛtāḥ",
      "translation": "\"But the second queen Sumati on part, oh, tigerly-man Rama, verily delivered a round and long egg which is like a single gourd, and on breaking it up sixty thousand sons are issued forth from that cucumber like egg.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
